BT /F1 11 Tf 56 760 Td 15 TL
(Neural Networks Basics - Lecture Notes) Tj T*
(CS 229 Intro to ML. Concepts, formulas, training process.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. The Perceptron) Tj T*
(A perceptron computes y = f\(w . x + b\): a weighted sum of inputs x) Tj T*
(with weights w and bias b, passed through activation function f.) Tj T*
(It is a linear classifier; the decision boundary is a hyperplane.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Activation Functions) Tj T*
(Sigmoid: s\(z\) = 1 / \(1 + e^-z\). Outputs in \(0,1\); saturates and) Tj T*
(causes vanishing gradients in deep nets.) Tj T*
(ReLU: f\(z\) = max\(0, z\). Cheap, sparse, the modern default; can) Tj T*
(suffer from 'dying ReLU' units.) Tj T*
(Tanh: outputs in \(-1,1\); zero-centred, still saturates.) Tj T*
(Softmax: converts logits into a probability distribution over) Tj T*
(classes; used in the output layer for classification.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. Loss Functions) Tj T*
(Mean squared error: L = \(1/n\) * sum\(\(y_pred - y_true\)^2\).) Tj T*
(Cross-entropy loss for classification: L = -sum\(y * log\(p\)\).) Tj T*
(The loss measures how wrong the network is; training minimises it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. Gradient Descent and Backpropagation) Tj T*
(Update rule: w <- w - lr * dL/dw, where lr is the learning rate.) Tj T*
(Backpropagation applies the chain rule to propagate the loss) Tj T*
(gradient from the output layer back to every weight.) Tj T*
(Variants: stochastic gradient descent \(SGD\), mini-batch GD, Adam.) Tj T*
(Learning rate too high -> divergence; too low -> slow convergence.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. Training Process \(standard pipeline\)) Tj T*
(Step 1: initialise weights randomly \(small values, symmetry break\).) Tj T*
(Step 2: forward pass - compute predictions for a batch.) Tj T*
(Step 3: compute the loss against the true labels.) Tj T*
(Step 4: backward pass - backpropagate gradients.) Tj T*
(Step 5: update weights with the optimiser.) Tj T*
(Step 6: repeat for many epochs; monitor validation loss.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Overfitting and Regularisation) Tj T*
(Overfitting: low training error, high validation error - the model) Tj T*
(memorises instead of generalising.) Tj T*
(Remedies: more data, dropout, L2 weight decay, early stopping.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. Self-check) Tj T*
(Q1. Why does a network of only linear layers collapse to one layer?) Tj T*
ET
